variable_typecast.pas:10:11: error: `Word(...)` here would treat a variable's bytes as `Word`: Turbo Pascal allows that for a variable of the same size, but Ruscal doesn't; use a `Word` variable instead, and assign between the two (only an untyped parameter can be seen as another type)
   Val(S, Word(I), N);
          ^^^^^^^

variable_typecast.pas:11:4: error: `Word(...)` here would treat a variable's bytes as `Word`: Turbo Pascal allows that for a variable of the same size, but Ruscal doesn't; use a `Word` variable instead, and assign between the two (only an untyped parameter can be seen as another type)
   Word(I) := 5;
   ^^^^^^^
